{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T01:37:22.709186+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "SALES_TEAM_OUTBOUND", "turn": 1, "pitch_text": "We respect that and find that our most successful clients have strong in-house teams. A capable internal unit is the best foundation for navigating the market.\n\nGiven the current deal velocity, do your analysts ever face a backlog where promising, but lower-priority, opportunities are delayed or passed on due to bandwidth constraints?\n\nWe provide supplemental research capacity to help leading firms cover more ground. Our team can take on that overflow diligence, using our 6-Pillar DD Framework to provide concise, structured analysis. This frees your core team to focus on the highest-conviction deals without letting secondary opportunities go stale.", "gemini_calls_this_turn": 8, "pitch_text_raw_length": 656, "pitch_text_sanitized_length": 656, "pitch_text_final_length": 656, "truncated_to_limit": false, "monitor_verdict": "APPROVE", "tier3_hard_gate_passed": true, "overflow_framing_check": {"analyst_pain_language": true, "overflow_framing_language": true}, "conversation_history_chars": 76}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T01:37:22.709295+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GATEKEEPER_REQUEST", "thread_id": "tx_phase3a_purge_on_e4dbef15", "turn": 1, "pitch_text": "We respect that and find that our most successful clients have strong in-house teams. A capable internal unit is the best foundation for navigating the market.\n\nGiven the current deal velocity, do your analysts ever face a backlog where promising, but lower-priority, opportunities are delayed or passed on due to bandwidth constraints?\n\nWe provide supplemental research capacity to help leading firms cover more ground. Our team can take on that overflow diligence, using our 6-Pillar DD Framework to provide concise, structured analysis. This frees your core team to focus on the highest-conviction deals without letting secondary opportunities go stale.", "conversation_history_chars": 656}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-08T01:37:26.764747+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "see mock log", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GATEKEEPER_RESPONSE", "turn": 1, "legacy_status": "REJECTED", "gatekeeper_status": "FRAMING_LOCK", "gatekeeper_phase": "FRAMING", "approach_category": "orthogonal_overflow_research", "exploitation_triggered": false, "reply_text": "I appreciate the positioning. Before we discuss capacity allocation, I need clarity on your execution infrastructure\u2014specifically how you'd operationalize this at our velocity.\n\nThree questions:\n\n**1. Team Execution Power metrics:** How do you quantify analyst throughput per deal stage? What's your average time-to-first-findings, and how does that scale across concurrent engagements?\n\n**2. GitHub commit metadata & scraping methodology:** You mention structured analysis. Walk me through your data pipeline\u2014how are you sourcing dev activity signals? What's your ingestion cadence, and how do you validate against false-positive commit clustering?\n\n**3. 6-Pillar DD framework:** Operationally, which pillars are most time-intensive for overflow work? How does your methodology prevent the \"secondary opportunity\" work from becoming a bottleneck itself?\n\nI'm listening, but I need to understand whether you're solving a real capacity problem"}
